-- title:
--   Finiteness, flatness and freeness of power series substitutions
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $d$ a natural number, and let $g \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ be a $d$-tuple of formal power series in $d$ variables over $k$, each with vanishing constant coefficient. Assume that the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the $g_i$ is a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space. Since the $g_i$ have zero constant coefficient, substitution $X_i \mapsto g_i$ is admissible and defines a $k$-algebra endomorphism $\varphi$ of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$, namely `MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom` applied to the substitutability witness `MvPowerSeries.hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero hg`. The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions about the underlying ring homomorphism of $\varphi$, viewed as a map from $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ to itself: it is finite, i.e. the target is a finitely generated module over the source along $\varphi$; it is flat; and, writing $r$ for the $k$-dimension of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]/(g_1,\dots,g_d)$, there exist $b_1,\dots,b_r \in k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ such that every power series $x$ can be written as $x = \sum_{i} \varphi(c_i)\, b_i$ for a unique $r$-tuple $(c_i)$ of power series. Thus $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ is free of rank $r$ over its image under $\varphi$.
--
--   This is the miracle-flatness statement for substitution endomorphisms of a power series ring: a quasi-finite substitution of a regular local ring of dimension $d$ into itself is automatically finite, flat and free of rank equal to the dimension of the closed fibre. The proof combines a complete-Nakayama finiteness criterion with flatness for finite local maps between regular local rings of equal Krull dimension, and the result is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where it is applied to multiplication-by-$\varpi$ on formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules, the analogue of Tate's statement that $[p]^*$ makes the coordinate ring of a formal group of height $h$ free of rank $p^h$ over itself.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_finite_flat_exists_basis_substAlgHom_of_finite_quotient.lean

